## 11. Agent Handoff Instructions

> This section is written for AI-assisted development teams or autonomous agents.
> It consolidates everything an agent needs to begin implementation without ambiguity.

### 11.1 Objective
> One paragraph summary of what needs to be built and why.

[Restate the core problem and solution in plain, unambiguous language. Avoid product jargon. Write as if the reader has no prior context.]

### 11.2 Inputs
> What does the agent/team receive as inputs to begin work?

- [ ] This PRD (requirements and acceptance criteria)
- [ ] Design assets: [Link]
- [ ] API documentation: [Link]
- [ ] Existing codebase context: [Repo / branch / folder]
- [ ] Test data / sandbox credentials: [Link or location]

### 11.3 Explicit Constraints
> Hard rules the agent must not violate under any circumstances.

- **Do not** store raw payment card data — tokenization is required
- **Do not** modify the existing [X] service — integrate via API only
- **Do not** deploy to production — deliver to staging environment only
- **Do not** introduce new external dependencies without approval
- [Add constraints specific to your environment]

### 11.4 Success Conditions
> The agent's work is complete when ALL of the following are true:

- [ ] All P0 requirements in Section 4 are implemented
- [ ] All P0 acceptance criteria in Section 5 are passing
- [ ] All TC-00X test cases in Section 10.1 pass
- [ ] No regressions in [existing feature / test suite]
- [ ] Code is documented and follows [style guide / conventions link]
- [ ] PR is submitted to [branch] with test results attached

### 11.5 Ambiguity Protocol
> What should the agent do when it encounters something not covered by this PRD?

1. Check the Open Questions log (Section 9) first
2. Default to the most conservative interpretation that satisfies the requirement
3. Flag the ambiguity in a comment in the PR — do not silently choose
4. Do not block on minor unknowns — implement with a clearly marked TODO

### 11.6 Handoff Checklist
> Agent completes this before marking work done.

- [ ] All success conditions met (Section 11.4)
- [ ] Open questions encountered during development logged in Section 9
- [ ] Test results filled into Section 10
- [ ] Any deviations from requirements documented with rationale
- [ ] Staging deployment confirmed and link provided

